WEBVTT

00:00:58.000 --> 00:01:01.030
<b>Skull-face Bookseller Honda-san</b>

00:01:02.510 --> 00:01:04.610
<b>Staff Picks</b>

00:01:02.510 --> 00:01:04.610
<b>Anime adaptations</b>

00:01:02.510 --> 00:01:04.610
<b>New books</b>

00:01:04.610 --> 00:01:07.390
<b>Released today</b>

00:01:04.610 --> 00:01:07.390
<b>Autographed Books</b>

00:01:04.610 --> 00:01:09.010
<b>Children's books</b>

00:01:04.610 --> 00:01:09.010
<b>Sale</b>

00:01:05.510 --> 00:01:09.000
<b>Books</b>

00:01:09.010 --> 00:01:12.980
<b>The Alternate <i>Skull-face 
Bookseller Honda-san</i></b>

00:01:12.980 --> 00:01:15.020
<b>Autographed books</b>

00:01:15.020 --> 00:01:17.710
<b>Books</b>

00:01:17.910 --> 00:01:20.850
Pardon me...

00:01:23.430 --> 00:01:27.090
You aren't selling the <i>Ju*p Comics</i>

00:01:27.090 --> 00:01:30.870
that goes on sale tomorrow early, are you?

00:01:30.870 --> 00:01:32.120
We aren't.

00:01:32.120 --> 00:01:33.940
It's on sale tomorrow.

00:01:36.610 --> 00:01:37.630
You suck!

00:01:38.370 --> 00:01:46.010
<b>Released Today</b>

00:01:39.640 --> 00:01:42.030
This shop oughta go out of business.

00:01:42.520 --> 00:01:46.010
Um... Are you okay?

00:01:46.400 --> 00:01:47.580
Yes.

00:01:47.580 --> 00:01:50.540
My apologies for the disruption.

00:01:51.150 --> 00:01:54.890
<b>Store staff</b>

00:01:53.090 --> 00:01:54.890
Ah, there you are.

00:01:55.160 --> 00:01:57.030
Good work, Honda.

00:01:57.030 --> 00:01:58.300
Good work.

00:01:58.800 --> 00:02:02.180
Sorry, a customer had me.

00:02:02.400 --> 00:02:04.800
We're getting a lot of inquiries today, huh?

00:02:04.800 --> 00:02:05.670
Yes.

00:02:05.670 --> 00:02:09.120
It's busy in the shop, 
so I was prepared, but...

00:02:09.920 --> 00:02:11.450
Oh, Honda-san.

00:02:11.450 --> 00:02:13.520
How was the shelf?

00:02:13.520 --> 00:02:15.540
Is something wrong?

00:02:15.540 --> 00:02:20.160
The books get moved on their own these days.

00:02:20.160 --> 00:02:24.220
I thought it might be due to 
shoplifting, so I had him patrol.

00:02:24.220 --> 00:02:25.050
Right.

00:02:25.050 --> 00:02:29.320
I saw someone who was suspicious 
earlier, but I lost sight of them.

00:02:29.320 --> 00:02:30.240
Really?

00:02:30.240 --> 00:02:31.520
What were they like?

00:02:31.520 --> 00:02:32.750
Um...

00:02:33.290 --> 00:02:36.810
It was a yokai with three eyes, 
an intense glare, and...

00:02:37.100 --> 00:02:41.740
He seemed more like a 
hitman than a shoplifter.

00:02:42.070 --> 00:02:45.510
He's been wandering around 
the shop the whole time.

00:02:48.570 --> 00:02:50.720
That's Shoplift G-Man.

00:02:50.720 --> 00:02:52.410
G-Man?!

00:02:54.110 --> 00:02:54.630
Hey.

00:02:54.630 --> 00:02:56.060
Good work out there.

00:02:56.060 --> 00:03:00.120
<i>I feel like his intensity makes 
him less effective as a patrol.</i>

00:03:00.890 --> 00:03:03.310
About the books that were misplaced...

00:03:03.310 --> 00:03:04.840
I found out why.

00:03:04.840 --> 00:03:06.880
So was it a shoplifter?

00:03:06.880 --> 00:03:08.890
No, it was a normal customer.

00:03:09.330 --> 00:03:12.860
Apparently they wanted to give it more 
exposure because they like the book.

00:03:09.330 --> 00:03:17.540
<b>This deserves to be noticed more...</b>

00:03:12.860 --> 00:03:14.990
Jeez, that's so confusing.

00:03:14.990 --> 00:03:16.790
Thanks, but no thanks.

00:03:17.660 --> 00:03:19.320
Also, unrelated to that,

00:03:19.320 --> 00:03:23.280
there was an unusual pile of books 
in the middle of the BL section.

00:03:23.280 --> 00:03:27.010
<i>You went into the BL 
section? With that stare?</i>

00:03:27.580 --> 00:03:30.550
There is a chance that a 
shoplifter tried to take them.

00:03:30.550 --> 00:03:31.930
Please be careful.

00:03:31.930 --> 00:03:33.740
U-Uh, excuse me...

00:03:34.120 --> 00:03:36.820
Chief Armor was holding those this morning.

00:03:34.120 --> 00:03:40.460
<b>Ding dong ding dong
 </b>(Come to the counter, please)

00:03:36.820 --> 00:03:40.250
She probably left them there in 
the middle of doing other work.

00:03:41.960 --> 00:03:44.130
Put them where they belong.

00:03:44.130 --> 00:03:46.960
T-Tell <i>her</i> that.

00:03:48.130 --> 00:03:51.380
So, where is said Section Chief?

00:03:51.830 --> 00:03:54.540
I saw her go behind the counter.

00:03:54.540 --> 00:04:00.140
<i>Again, this is something we 
ask of all of our customers.</i>

00:04:00.960 --> 00:04:03.010
It's <i>that</i> guy again.

00:04:03.010 --> 00:04:04.180
Ah.

00:04:05.330 --> 00:04:07.030
As this is a popular product,

00:04:07.030 --> 00:04:11.190
we kindly ask that each 
customer purchases only one.

00:04:11.590 --> 00:04:15.940
I'm quite the regular customer, aren't I?

00:04:16.380 --> 00:04:18.880
At least, I thought so.

00:04:19.200 --> 00:04:22.510
Though I don't know how you feel about me.

00:04:23.510 --> 00:04:26.630
I can't say I like being treated the same way

00:04:26.630 --> 00:04:29.420
as all the other customers.

00:04:29.850 --> 00:04:30.930
C'mon.

00:04:31.240 --> 00:04:32.150
I'm buying them.

00:04:32.790 --> 00:04:35.970
I can't accept the way you're treating me.

00:04:37.710 --> 00:04:40.090
He's talking crazy.

00:04:40.090 --> 00:04:44.530
He wasn't <i>this</i> weird before.

00:04:45.320 --> 00:04:48.830
I don't think he can even
 realizes it anymore.

00:04:50.030 --> 00:04:51.880
I called the department head, though.

00:04:51.880 --> 00:04:52.880
They said they're coming.

00:04:52.880 --> 00:04:53.880
Oh, good.

00:04:53.880 --> 00:04:55.360
That's a relief.

00:04:55.920 --> 00:04:57.600
Wait, that's bad!

00:05:01.390 --> 00:05:02.920
Section Chief Armor!

00:05:03.610 --> 00:05:06.220
I guess I should tell you...

00:05:06.220 --> 00:05:11.300
I'd like copies that neither you nor 
other customers have touched!

00:05:11.580 --> 00:05:16.070
I do tend to be pretty picky 
about that kind of thing!

00:05:16.280 --> 00:05:19.450
Shoot, he's scaring the other customers away!

00:05:19.450 --> 00:05:20.870
That bastard...

00:05:20.870 --> 00:05:23.000
Is there nothing we can do?

00:05:23.000 --> 00:05:24.290
It's no use.

00:05:24.290 --> 00:05:25.450
He's a regular here.

00:05:25.450 --> 00:05:28.540
He's not going to listen to 
the staff he recognizes.

00:05:29.000 --> 00:05:36.600
<b>Abracadabra! Hurgleburgle! Wharrgarble!</b>

00:05:29.140 --> 00:05:31.900
Then let's get Assistant Manager 
Majutsushi to go out as a customer

00:05:31.900 --> 00:05:33.760
and fight him, since he doesn't know him.

00:05:33.760 --> 00:05:35.750
I don't know how to ask him.

00:05:36.920 --> 00:05:38.840
With all due respect,

00:05:38.840 --> 00:05:42.460
any more and you're going to 
disturb the other customers.

00:05:42.460 --> 00:05:44.610
Disturb them? Me?

00:05:45.420 --> 00:05:52.070
I don't appreciate that kind of language!

00:05:52.790 --> 00:05:54.350
Section Chief!

00:06:01.170 --> 00:06:04.890
Sir, I apologize for the long wait.

00:06:06.230 --> 00:06:08.130
<b>Manga Department Head
 Tengai</b>

00:06:06.790 --> 00:06:12.940
I'm the manga department head, Tengai.

00:06:14.180 --> 00:06:18.580
It would be my pleasure to 
assist you from here on.

00:06:19.970 --> 00:06:21.420
Right.

00:06:21.420 --> 00:06:23.470
You'd called in the department head.

00:06:23.470 --> 00:06:26.760
Thank goodness for our department head.

00:06:26.760 --> 00:06:28.680
Cool, back to work.

00:06:35.960 --> 00:06:40.970
<b>End</b>

00:06:40.970 --> 00:06:43.970
<b>You Can Quit Your Job Whenever You Want</b>

00:06:43.970 --> 00:06:47.100
<b>Staff Only</b>

00:06:45.070 --> 00:06:46.170
<i>Sold out?!</i>

00:06:46.170 --> 00:06:47.180
<i>What the hell?</i>

00:06:47.180 --> 00:06:49.530
<i>How can you run out so quickly?</i>

00:06:49.530 --> 00:06:53.480
My apologies, that book happens 
to be extremely popular.

00:06:53.480 --> 00:06:54.990
<i>Unbelievable!</i>

00:06:54.990 --> 00:06:57.710
<i>You'd better be paying for 
my time and phone bills.</i>

00:06:57.710 --> 00:06:59.420
<i>You can't, can you?</i>

00:06:59.420 --> 00:07:01.420
I'm very sorry.

00:07:01.420 --> 00:07:03.770
<i>I'm never buying from 
your crappy store again!</i>

00:07:06.640 --> 00:07:08.190
Are you all right?

00:07:08.190 --> 00:07:10.180
Yeah, I guess.

00:07:11.760 --> 00:07:13.910
No, honestly, I was scared shitless.

00:07:13.910 --> 00:07:15.040
There, there.

00:07:15.040 --> 00:07:16.380
You did good.

00:07:16.830 --> 00:07:22.940
Honestly, I wasn't sure when I would 
just softly hang up the phone.

00:07:17.770 --> 00:07:24.610
<b>I want to become a clam...</b>

00:07:22.940 --> 00:07:24.060
<i>That's</i> what scared you?

00:07:26.060 --> 00:07:28.870
<i>That's hyperbole, of course,</i>

00:07:30.080 --> 00:07:34.430
<i>but it's true that I become wary
 about customer questions</i>

00:07:34.430 --> 00:07:37.120
<i>when I get those calls.</i>

00:07:37.120 --> 00:07:39.230
Pardon me.

00:07:39.230 --> 00:07:40.060
Yes?

00:07:40.060 --> 00:07:43.220
I'm looking for this book.

00:07:43.830 --> 00:07:47.600
This book is probably in another section.

00:07:47.600 --> 00:07:49.380
Shall I have it brought over?

00:07:49.380 --> 00:07:52.240
Oh, which section is it?

00:07:52.240 --> 00:07:54.370
I can go there myself.

00:07:55.250 --> 00:07:57.440
It's been a long time since 
I've been at a bookstore.

00:07:57.440 --> 00:07:59.170
I'm so excited.

00:07:59.170 --> 00:08:00.980
Oh, really?

00:08:02.070 --> 00:08:05.680
I drop by every now and then, and every time,

00:08:05.980 --> 00:08:08.390
I'm reminded that I love bookstores.

00:08:08.390 --> 00:08:10.520
You must be the same way.

00:08:13.060 --> 00:08:15.130
<i>I can't cry at the storefront!</i>

00:08:23.730 --> 00:08:27.340
<b>Sob sob sob</b>

00:08:24.080 --> 00:08:25.210
What's wrong, Honda?!

00:08:25.210 --> 00:08:27.030
Did you get pollen allergies 
alone somehow?!

00:08:27.340 --> 00:08:29.950
I just had a terrifying customer,

00:08:29.950 --> 00:08:33.640
and then a saintly one right 
after, and I lost myself.

00:08:34.160 --> 00:08:35.340
Oh, you scared me.

00:08:35.870 --> 00:08:37.990
I get that, though.

00:08:37.990 --> 00:08:42.240
Nice customers have awesome 
healing properties.

00:08:42.240 --> 00:08:43.350
Yup.

00:08:45.650 --> 00:08:47.250
There, there, have a drink.

00:08:47.250 --> 00:08:48.640
Have some of my chocolates.

00:08:48.640 --> 00:08:50.210
Thank you.

00:08:52.880 --> 00:08:55.830
You can quit work whenever you want.

00:08:56.000 --> 00:08:59.160
You don't have to do anything that'll make 
you so miserable that you wanna cry.

00:08:59.160 --> 00:09:00.430
Totally.

00:09:00.630 --> 00:09:06.200
So it's when the healing stops working 
that it's time to move on, I guess.

00:09:07.400 --> 00:09:09.090
Did you know, Kami-chan?

00:09:09.090 --> 00:09:13.470
"You can whenever you want" is 
the same as "You never will."

00:09:13.470 --> 00:09:16.080
Hey, that's not fair.

00:09:17.020 --> 00:09:18.310
Ah, there you are.

00:09:18.650 --> 00:09:21.200
Honda-san, a customer's looking for you.

00:09:21.200 --> 00:09:22.390
Oh, okay.

00:09:22.390 --> 00:09:23.850
I'll be right there.

00:09:24.770 --> 00:09:27.130
Oh, there you are, sir!

00:09:27.390 --> 00:09:29.630
Look, I bought it!

00:09:29.630 --> 00:09:32.300
Thank you so much!

00:09:32.500 --> 00:09:34.280
I just wanted to thank you.

00:09:34.280 --> 00:09:37.770
Sorry to waste your time.

00:09:37.770 --> 00:09:39.480
<i>No...</i>

00:09:39.480 --> 00:09:42.650
<i>You came back just to tell me?</i>

00:09:43.030 --> 00:09:44.650
<i>She's too nice.</i>

00:09:44.650 --> 00:09:45.870
<i>Oh, no.</i>

00:09:46.510 --> 00:09:51.740
<i>What if I get another terrifying 
customer after so much kindness?</i>

00:09:57.920 --> 00:10:00.440
You're way too negative!

00:10:00.440 --> 00:10:01.400
But...

00:10:01.400 --> 00:10:04.120
It's easier to be thankful if you 
expect the customers to be terrible,

00:10:04.120 --> 00:10:06.890
but they turn out to be nice.

00:10:06.890 --> 00:10:08.840
What are you, a professional edgelord?

00:10:12.600 --> 00:10:17.580
<i>I don't like putting myself 
in scary situations.</i>

00:10:19.080 --> 00:10:20.160
Welcome.

00:10:20.160 --> 00:10:21.820
Thank you for waiting.

00:10:22.620 --> 00:10:26.500
<i>But when the bell goes off, 
I've already forgotten.</i>
